  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nAs the hurricane int he Gulf moves off to the east, and the\nhurricanes in the Pacific reinforce the upper trough across the\nwestern US, upper level ridge builds across the Plains for the\nweekend into next week. Temperatures climb with highs forecasted\nto climb well into the low to mid 90s (or roughly 10+ degrees \nabove normal) by Tuesday or Wednesday.\n\nEnd of next week has more uncertainty, and will depend on how far\neast the West Coast upper trough shifts east towards the Plains\nand Southern Rockies. Many of the models and their ensembles show\nsome version of a shortwave rotating southwest to northeast across\nthe area late week, but that timing and strength remain uncertain.\nWave may be accompanied with at least scattered convection, but\nwhether that stays out along the Texas/New Mexico border or\nfarther east into West Central Texas remains a big question. Not\ngoing to argue with the blends at this point, which indicated\nscattered POP chances along with enough cloud cover to keep\ntemperatures down a few degrees.",
